WEBVTT

00:11.470 --> 00:17.340
Yuke Feldio, stop the Twilight King
and destroy the gold.

00:17.880 --> 00:23.570
Should you fail, this world will be
swallowed by the twilight as well.

00:24.250 --> 00:26.800
Yes. Yuke Feldio,

00:26.800 --> 00:30.990
you will become the hero
and save this world!

00:39.130 --> 00:46.090
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:01.000 --> 02:01.550
(Episode 13: Biblion, the Book Spirit)

02:01.550 --> 02:04.630
(Episode 13: Biblion, the Book Spirit)
Hero? Come on, give me a break.

02:04.920 --> 02:07.050
(Episode 13: Biblion, the Book Spirit)
Someone has to do it,

02:07.490 --> 02:10.010
and not just anyone will do.

02:10.440 --> 02:11.510
Yes, but...

02:11.510 --> 02:13.430
If you won't do it,

02:13.430 --> 02:17.260
I'll raise another Clover member
to rank A and have them do it.

02:18.200 --> 02:20.200
Has that motivated you a bit?

02:20.970 --> 02:23.220
You so closely resemble a young Saga,

02:23.220 --> 02:26.400
but compared to him,
you're a bit on the prudish side.

02:26.970 --> 02:28.780
You know my uncle?

02:29.920 --> 02:31.590
He's an old friend.

02:31.590 --> 02:33.980
A man brimming with
intuition and confidence,

02:33.980 --> 02:37.000
with the talent to back it all up.

02:37.000 --> 02:38.790
He was a fine adventurer.

02:39.210 --> 02:42.900
In all seriousness,
I'd be grateful if you'd accept.

02:42.900 --> 02:44.670
I'll give you all the support I can.

02:44.670 --> 02:47.300
Aren't you expecting a bit too much of me?

02:47.620 --> 02:48.860
Call it intuition.

02:49.480 --> 02:52.800
On top of that, you were chosen
by a priestess from another world.

02:54.030 --> 02:56.060
Give me some time to think about it.

02:56.450 --> 02:57.790
Of course.

02:57.790 --> 03:00.120
Still, a prompt answer
would be preferable.

03:00.120 --> 03:01.060
Understand?

03:01.650 --> 03:03.310
I'll consult with my partymates.

03:03.920 --> 03:06.680
Well, if my intuition is correct,

03:06.680 --> 03:09.520
your misgivings will be
cleared away soon enough.

03:09.520 --> 03:13.320
Also... there are things only you can do.

03:18.490 --> 03:20.460
A hero? That's amazing!

03:20.790 --> 03:22.890
It's too much to ask of me.

03:23.770 --> 03:26.090
If it's stressful for you, tell him no.

03:27.480 --> 03:31.090
He said if I do that, he'll make
another member of Clover do it.

03:31.380 --> 03:34.340
Marina, maybe? That's a problem.

03:35.160 --> 03:40.790
I don't mind giving the twilight city
Glad Shi-im another go,

03:40.790 --> 03:45.830
but asking me to save the world
from crisis is just too much.

03:45.830 --> 03:50.610
Yeah... but Rune did call
you by name, didn't she?

03:50.610 --> 03:52.870
There must be some meaning to it.

03:52.870 --> 03:53.490
Meaning?

03:53.490 --> 03:59.110
Yeah. Only you can do it, and
you're the only one she can ask,

03:59.110 --> 04:00.620
so she was waiting for you.

04:01.050 --> 04:02.930
Only I can do it?

04:04.720 --> 04:09.250
I think all you need to do is be
the adventurer you've always been.

04:09.250 --> 04:13.360
I get it. World in crisis
or not, hero or not,

04:13.360 --> 04:16.450
in the end, what I need to
do is the same as always.

04:17.070 --> 04:19.480
Thanks. I feel so much lighter.

04:19.480 --> 04:21.140
You're welcome.

04:23.250 --> 04:26.900
It's okay. No matter what
happens, I'm on your side.

04:27.390 --> 04:30.910
Even if the world falls and
everyone else is gone,

04:30.910 --> 04:32.990
I'll be by your side until the end.

04:35.640 --> 04:36.240
Hmm?

04:36.680 --> 04:37.900
Nothing.

04:37.900 --> 04:41.190
I can only cling to you like this
when you're worried about something.

04:42.090 --> 04:44.540
That's when you don't get shy or run away.

04:45.630 --> 04:47.290
Have I made you feel uneasy?

04:47.290 --> 04:50.550
It's okay. You still came to talk to me.

04:50.550 --> 04:53.100
And I'm sure the others
will feel the same.

04:53.100 --> 04:56.300
We're all a lot stronger than you think.

04:57.030 --> 05:01.060
I know you are. But it still worries me.

05:01.660 --> 05:05.310
That's exactly what
we love about you, Yuke.

05:08.190 --> 05:10.690
(A Few Days Later)

05:12.750 --> 05:16.700
And that's the outline of the new
joint mission that's been announced.

05:16.700 --> 05:21.720
I'd like the parties Scordia,
Fullbound, Carmine, and Clover

05:21.720 --> 05:24.380
to fulfill the conditions
to seal Glad Shi-im

05:24.380 --> 05:26.620
and get us past this challenge.

05:26.620 --> 05:29.560
And while we will have
you stream your attempt,

05:29.560 --> 05:31.380
viewership will be limited.

05:31.680 --> 05:33.920
Specifically, only certain members of

05:33.920 --> 05:37.510
the academy and Adventurer's Guild
will be permitted to watch.

05:37.510 --> 05:41.710
If any more people lose their
minds to that twilight glow,

05:41.710 --> 05:43.640
things are going to get out of hand.

05:43.940 --> 05:45.680
Any questions?

05:46.520 --> 05:47.700
Yes, Zaccard.

05:48.860 --> 05:52.570
Why does a C-rank party like Clover
get to continue the mission?

05:52.920 --> 05:55.160
They succeeded in investigating
Achromatic Darkness,

05:55.160 --> 05:57.840
the toughest dungeon we know.

05:57.840 --> 06:00.380
They have also produced
results in this mission

06:00.380 --> 06:03.700
and have earned provisional
A-rank status for its duration.

06:04.040 --> 06:06.380
Huh? What the hell?

06:06.380 --> 06:10.460
They only went through a few
floors of Achromatic Darkness!

06:10.460 --> 06:13.400
We could handle that, no problem!

06:13.400 --> 06:16.210
I'll have to disagree with you on that.

06:16.560 --> 06:21.150
I don't know how familiar Fullbound
is with dungeon conquest,

06:21.150 --> 06:24.010
but if you attempt Achromatic Darkness
with that attitude,

06:24.010 --> 06:25.470
it'll only end in tragedy.

06:25.470 --> 06:29.890
What?! You sayin' we're not as
good as that stupid Red Mage?

06:29.890 --> 06:31.770
That's enough.

06:31.770 --> 06:32.210
(Carmine Leader, Marona)

06:32.210 --> 06:35.530
(Carmine Leader, Marona)
Aren't we supposed to be an alliance
facing this challenge together?

06:35.530 --> 06:39.330
It's true that Clover has a
bit less experience than us.

06:39.330 --> 06:42.790
Can't we just take that to mean
the rest of us have it easier?

06:42.790 --> 06:45.900
We just need to produce results
on this job. Am I wrong?

06:45.900 --> 06:48.320
Hmph! No need to tell me that!

06:52.190 --> 06:53.880
Ah, youth!

06:53.880 --> 06:56.670
Well, better to have that
fighting spirit than not.

06:57.000 --> 07:00.170
I apologize for making the
situation uncomfortable.

07:00.480 --> 07:03.640
We'll be depending on you, Lucent.

07:03.640 --> 07:08.220
There aren't many who've come back
alive from Achromatic Darkness.

07:08.620 --> 07:10.730
We will put in our utmost effort.

07:10.730 --> 07:12.550
See ya in the dungeon.

07:17.240 --> 07:22.110
You were right to ask me to keep
that hero business secret.

07:22.650 --> 07:26.340
This would've been even messier
if Zaccard knew about that.

07:26.340 --> 07:26.990
Agreed.

07:27.450 --> 07:33.800
Also, I've been told that the equipment
Rain requested is nearly done.

07:33.800 --> 07:35.380
Thank you.

07:35.380 --> 07:37.000
So, think you can pull it off?

07:37.000 --> 07:38.880
I'll do everything I can.

07:39.340 --> 07:41.010
We'll look forward to good news,

07:41.400 --> 07:44.010
Hero Yuke Feldio.

07:49.000 --> 07:51.780
Even with all the information
from the other parties,

07:51.780 --> 07:55.150
I still don't know how to
get into Vordan Castle.

07:56.000 --> 07:59.150
I think we should have Rune help us.

08:00.080 --> 08:01.150
Rune?

08:01.440 --> 08:04.910
She seems to have something
to do with Glad Shi-im.

08:07.280 --> 08:09.160
- Wait up!
- I agree that the castle might
open its gate for her, but...

08:09.160 --> 08:11.170
- Uh-oh, you're within reach!
- I agree that the castle might
open its gate for her, but...

08:11.170 --> 08:12.660
- I agree that the castle might
open its gate for her, but...

08:13.010 --> 08:15.000
I realize it's dangerous,

08:15.000 --> 08:20.670
but there's something telling me
that we should take her along.

08:21.000 --> 08:24.100
It's unusual for you to
rely so much on intuition.

08:24.100 --> 08:25.930
I don't really get it, either.

08:26.760 --> 08:28.430
Yuke, you have a visitor!

08:29.030 --> 08:30.180
A visitor?

08:30.520 --> 08:32.020
Come on in!

08:32.020 --> 08:33.750
Pardon me.

08:33.750 --> 08:38.040
I wanted to consult with you
about our course of action...

08:38.040 --> 08:40.320
What's wrong? Is there a problem?

08:40.320 --> 08:41.190
Take that!

08:42.000 --> 08:43.320
Well done!

08:43.320 --> 08:45.820
Here it comes, Rune!

08:47.680 --> 08:51.300
All right. We'll guard Niberune, as well.

08:51.300 --> 08:52.620
Will that do?

08:52.620 --> 08:53.700
Huh?

08:54.030 --> 08:58.090
The king should consider the
Golden Priestess a guest of honor.

08:58.570 --> 09:00.900
If it doesn't work, we can withdraw.

09:00.900 --> 09:02.280
Yes, but...

09:02.280 --> 09:05.120
Yuke, you must understand.

09:05.120 --> 09:08.430
If she were connected to Glad Shi-im,

09:08.430 --> 09:11.110
you wouldn't have been able to
remove her from the dungeon.

09:12.030 --> 09:16.610
In other words, this dungeon is
already in a dangerous enough state

09:16.610 --> 09:18.850
to cause an artificial Overflow.

09:19.480 --> 09:22.610
There's no telling when the
Stampede might happen.

09:23.160 --> 09:26.400
There is little time remaining.

09:28.280 --> 09:31.530
All right. We'll take Niberune with us.

09:31.530 --> 09:32.870
Hey... Huh?

09:40.760 --> 09:43.050
Sure is a strange city.

09:43.750 --> 09:47.170
Damn it! Where the hell's the
entrance s'posed to be?!

09:57.270 --> 09:59.980
I see. So this is Loge.

09:59.980 --> 10:00.350
(Scordia, Mage/Alchemist Moria)

10:00.350 --> 10:03.980
(Scordia, Mage/Alchemist Moria)
So it wasn't a group hallucination after all.

10:04.280 --> 10:07.270
Welcome home, Lady Niberune.

10:07.270 --> 10:09.780
How were things on the outside?

10:11.640 --> 10:13.030
Who are you?

10:13.030 --> 10:16.950
Oh, dear. You have forgotten me?

10:16.950 --> 10:21.540
No, no. It's better if
you forget everything.

10:22.360 --> 10:26.920
Loge, the Golden Priestess said
to make you tell us everything.

10:26.920 --> 10:30.320
So tell us. What is happening here?

10:30.320 --> 10:32.550
What will happen to our world?

10:32.870 --> 10:36.820
So the honored one entrusted
you with this, then?

10:36.820 --> 10:41.060
There is little that this
aged man can tell you.

10:41.400 --> 10:46.690
That said, if Lady Niberune is
with you, perhaps you will learn.

10:56.150 --> 10:57.290
This way.

10:57.860 --> 11:00.160
Where are you taking us?

11:00.160 --> 11:03.670
To a place where you can
learn what you wish to know.

11:04.000 --> 11:07.480
If this is a trap, we don't want
to walk into it all at once.

11:07.480 --> 11:09.300
Moria, come with me.

11:10.940 --> 11:14.470
Miriam, run and tell the
other parties about this.

11:14.470 --> 11:14.790
(Scordia, Thief/Mage Miriam)

11:14.790 --> 11:16.720
(Scordia, Thief/Mage Miriam)
Understood. I will go at once.

11:17.560 --> 11:19.600
Darcas and Maje, wait here.

11:21.820 --> 11:22.690
Let's go.

11:36.600 --> 11:38.870
It's okay. We're all here.

11:39.400 --> 11:40.150
Yeah.

11:41.390 --> 11:43.950
It feels as if the place is rejecting us.

11:43.950 --> 11:46.750
Really wears on the old bones.

11:47.360 --> 11:48.800
Rejecting...

11:48.800 --> 11:52.470
That's what this is.
The sense of rejection.

11:52.470 --> 11:53.260
Yeah.

12:00.920 --> 12:02.390
Please enter.

12:02.680 --> 12:05.310
This is the royal archive.

12:07.310 --> 12:08.270
Wow!

12:08.590 --> 12:11.690
I've never seen so many books before!

12:15.340 --> 12:19.320
I thought perhaps you might find
the information you need here.

12:19.320 --> 12:23.210
Sadly, I'm a poor speaker.

12:23.510 --> 12:24.980
No, I think not.

12:24.980 --> 12:30.210
You're avoiding saying something
out loud, thus acknowledging it.

12:32.710 --> 12:34.260
What do you mean?

12:34.750 --> 12:39.100
Yuke, as a humble mage yourself,
you must understand.

12:39.650 --> 12:41.720
Words are begotten by acknowledgment,

12:41.720 --> 12:45.600
and mana transforms powerful
words into phenomena.

12:45.600 --> 12:50.220
Within this man resides either
very strong mana or a curse.

12:50.220 --> 12:53.740
So strong that it prevents him
from voicing things directly.

12:54.160 --> 12:56.240
Um... So you mean...

12:56.800 --> 12:59.320
He wants to speak,

12:59.320 --> 13:02.680
and he hid the things he
wants to say in here.

13:06.390 --> 13:10.490
Lucent, those red books there,
bring them all to me.

13:10.490 --> 13:11.500
All right.

13:13.320 --> 13:16.040
Young lady, can you read?

13:16.040 --> 13:17.770
Yeah, no problem!

13:17.770 --> 13:19.020
Very good.

13:19.020 --> 13:23.720
Let us get to the true pleasure of
adventuring: the acquisition of knowledge.

13:23.720 --> 13:26.350
Focusing all mana on detection.

13:26.350 --> 13:27.980
Sense Distortion.

13:27.980 --> 13:29.230
(Sense Distortion)

13:30.580 --> 13:31.730
Um...

13:32.120 --> 13:35.400
That big book with the brown spine.

13:35.400 --> 13:36.240
And...

13:36.240 --> 13:38.490
Something's strange
about that desk drawer.

13:38.830 --> 13:40.270
I'll check it out!

13:40.270 --> 13:41.740
I'll get the book!

13:44.430 --> 13:45.250
Silk?

13:45.570 --> 13:47.730
There are unusual spirits here.

13:47.730 --> 13:50.500
They may be unique to Glad Shi-im.

13:50.810 --> 13:52.130
What are they like?

13:52.690 --> 13:55.510
It's difficult to put into words...

13:55.840 --> 13:57.750
but rather than natural phenomena,

13:57.750 --> 14:00.560
they feel more like memories,
or songs, or... traditions?

14:00.560 --> 14:03.010
Like they're connected to people's minds.

14:03.560 --> 14:05.520
I'll try to make contact.

14:16.540 --> 14:19.560
Oh, it's a book spirit!

14:19.560 --> 14:22.410
It dwells in things that
hold stories and memories.

14:22.830 --> 14:26.210
I'll collect information
from this little one.

14:26.210 --> 14:28.020
Okay. Rain?

14:28.020 --> 14:29.040
Right.

14:29.880 --> 14:34.400
Hmm, I see... This is... Hmm?

14:37.930 --> 14:40.260
There was a key in the desk drawer.

14:40.260 --> 14:42.220
It's probably for this book!

14:42.580 --> 14:45.220
Loge, do you know what this book is?

14:45.500 --> 14:48.100
Yes, of course I do.

14:48.410 --> 14:50.350
It's nothing dangerous, right?

14:50.710 --> 14:54.860
I'm afraid these lips cannot
say whether it is or not.

14:55.160 --> 14:59.190
No. Tell me that
this book isn't dangerous.

15:01.390 --> 15:03.570
I need to hear it from your mouth.

15:05.570 --> 15:09.200
Correct. There is no danger in this book.

15:12.140 --> 15:14.960
Looks like it just turned safe.

15:15.270 --> 15:17.960
Sorry. Was I forcing you?

15:18.310 --> 15:19.970
No, not at all.

15:20.410 --> 15:22.020
Okay, I'm opening it.

15:24.790 --> 15:26.810
Is this a grimoire?

15:26.810 --> 15:28.100
Looks like it.

15:28.100 --> 15:31.230
It has a bunch of similar
magic formulas overlapping.

15:31.230 --> 15:33.280
I think they're a bit different, though.

15:33.280 --> 15:35.360
These two are different right here,

15:35.780 --> 15:38.840
and this is this flipped
upside-down... I think.

15:38.840 --> 15:40.610
This looks really difficult.

15:40.610 --> 15:43.020
I don't get it at all!

15:43.020 --> 15:44.490
Neither do I.

15:44.490 --> 15:48.570
I don't, either. If only we
could read it somehow...

15:48.570 --> 15:51.750
I think I might be able to help.

15:51.750 --> 15:54.070
Silk, you're ready now?

15:54.070 --> 15:56.130
Yes, we've become friends.

15:56.130 --> 15:58.500
What? It's so much smaller!

15:58.500 --> 16:00.040
How cute!

16:00.040 --> 16:03.560
If we have this little one help,
I think we can figure it out.

16:03.560 --> 16:04.850
Really?

16:04.850 --> 16:07.750
Yes. Master, put your hand here.

16:18.970 --> 16:19.530
Whoa...

16:22.920 --> 16:24.280
That was quite a surprise!

16:25.080 --> 16:26.400
Where are we?

16:26.400 --> 16:30.290
Atop the book. Inside the book.
Alongside memories.

16:34.120 --> 16:37.250
This is Biblion, the book spirit.

16:37.250 --> 16:41.130
I think Elementals of the past called
upon him to watch over this library.

16:41.480 --> 16:42.840
Biblion?

16:43.110 --> 16:45.470
Silk, this man is good.

16:45.810 --> 16:48.470
I know. He's my teacher!

16:48.720 --> 16:51.200
This book is a bit dangerous.

16:51.200 --> 16:52.350
Be cautious.

16:52.670 --> 16:54.450
We want to know what it says.

16:54.450 --> 16:56.350
Biblion, what should we do?

16:56.670 --> 16:59.060
To read is the way of man.

16:59.060 --> 17:01.610
I will interpret it in our way.
Understand?

17:01.890 --> 17:05.610
What does that mean?
Reading it isn't the right thing to do?

17:05.960 --> 17:08.190
We interpret and convey.

17:08.190 --> 17:10.120
Man can read, but not convey.

17:10.430 --> 17:12.350
That's fine, Biblion.

17:12.350 --> 17:14.250
But just tell me, please.

17:14.250 --> 17:16.620
Silk doesn't have any knowledge of magic.

17:16.950 --> 17:18.630
Yuke. Are you ready?

17:18.960 --> 17:20.380
Yes. Go ahead.

17:20.680 --> 17:22.830
Silk, watch over me.

17:22.830 --> 17:23.880
I will.

17:24.220 --> 17:26.130
Biblion, do it.

17:26.480 --> 17:27.890
It shall be done.

17:40.520 --> 17:43.030
Who are you? What are you doing?

17:48.350 --> 17:50.140
Okay. I understand.

17:55.600 --> 17:56.930
Are you all right?

17:57.650 --> 17:59.330
Did you find anything out?

18:00.360 --> 18:03.050
This grimoire is similar
to a technical book.

18:03.620 --> 18:08.050
The author was studying something called
the "Multi-Destruct Magic Formula."

18:08.350 --> 18:09.670
Multi...

18:09.670 --> 18:10.630
Destruct?

18:10.630 --> 18:11.430
What's that?

18:11.820 --> 18:15.930
A technique that causes a chain reaction
of multiple spells... I think.

18:16.450 --> 18:20.940
It's not combining spells to cast them
simultaneously, like my Prismatic Missile.

18:21.290 --> 18:22.850
It's like a domino effect.

18:22.850 --> 18:26.150
You initiate, destroy, and
rebuild many spells in turn

18:26.150 --> 18:30.300
to make them yield a single,
shared outcome.

18:30.300 --> 18:33.450
It lets you bring about a monstrously
huge outcome using magic.

18:33.760 --> 18:35.130
Um...

18:35.130 --> 18:36.200
I get it!

18:36.200 --> 18:37.250
You get what?!

18:37.250 --> 18:39.970
That is most intriguing.

18:39.970 --> 18:40.710
Moria?

18:41.140 --> 18:43.340
Have you finished deciphering your book?

18:43.340 --> 18:45.510
This appears to be a history book.

18:45.510 --> 18:50.590
It explains how Glad Shi-im
reached the state it's in now.

18:51.010 --> 18:55.810
It seems Glad Shi-im was the royal
capital of a country in another world.

18:55.810 --> 18:58.460
There were many gods living
all over this world,

18:58.460 --> 19:02.010
at times fighting with humans
and at times loving them

19:02.010 --> 19:04.360
as they built the age they lived in.

19:04.360 --> 19:08.410
But then their world was destroyed
in an event called "Sunset,"

19:08.410 --> 19:12.110
which is what we would think of
as the culling in this world.

19:12.490 --> 19:17.240
The people of this city and
King Vordan excelled at magic,

19:17.240 --> 19:21.120
and they came up with a plan
to escape their dying world.

19:21.430 --> 19:23.630
Escape it? So that's why...

19:24.240 --> 19:25.750
What is it, Yuke?

19:26.240 --> 19:28.860
The magic described in this grimoire is,

19:28.860 --> 19:31.760
frankly speaking,
magic that grants wishes.

19:32.060 --> 19:37.510
Ah. Not dimension-crossing magic
or mass evacuation magic, then?

19:37.510 --> 19:40.940
The mage who wrote this
grimoire didn't want that.

19:40.940 --> 19:43.210
He was after a solution
to the root problem—

19:43.210 --> 19:46.350
a way to overcome the culling.
That's what I think.

19:46.350 --> 19:49.280
And what became of that magic?

19:49.280 --> 19:52.190
He wasn't able to get sufficient results.

19:52.190 --> 19:55.440
No... His wish itself was granted, but...

19:56.300 --> 19:58.730
I don't want to stay here too long.

19:58.730 --> 20:01.210
I'll explain in more detail
after we get back.

20:01.210 --> 20:06.990
Of course. I let my guard down
here in this forest of knowledge.

20:06.990 --> 20:11.220
Yuke, might we compare the information
we've found upon our return?

20:11.220 --> 20:13.480
Of course, Moria.

20:13.480 --> 20:17.000
Yuke, tell me
what was in the grimoire, too.

20:17.000 --> 20:17.720
I will.

20:18.660 --> 20:20.470
So this is where y'all were.

20:20.850 --> 20:21.980
Find somethin'?

20:22.340 --> 20:24.220
We learned a few things.

20:24.220 --> 20:28.500
We're going to pull back now
to take home what we've found.

20:28.500 --> 20:29.360
What will you do?

20:29.800 --> 20:31.940
We'll head back, too, then.

20:32.290 --> 20:33.450
And Fullbound?

20:33.450 --> 20:36.040
They headed farther in.

20:36.040 --> 20:37.700
Should I have stopped 'em?

20:38.750 --> 20:41.180
No, let's leave that to them.

20:41.180 --> 20:44.840
We have Niberune. I want to
get back to camp quickly.

20:44.840 --> 20:48.460
Yeah. We can't take Rune with
us to chase after them.

20:48.460 --> 20:50.080
I agree.

20:50.080 --> 20:53.220
We'll join the guard mission on
the way back. You can relax.

20:53.220 --> 20:55.720
Thank you, Marona!

20:59.720 --> 21:03.490
Hey, Rune, let's have a bath
together when we get back.

21:03.490 --> 21:03.980
Okay!

21:03.980 --> 21:05.910
I'll join you, too!

21:05.910 --> 21:06.820
I will, too.

21:06.820 --> 21:07.460
And me.

21:07.460 --> 21:09.850
I'll have a bath with all of you!

21:10.860 --> 21:15.860
King Vordan used the gold
to grant just one wish...

21:15.860 --> 21:19.620
and the Glad Shi-im we see
here is the result of that?

22:56.050 --> 22:57.350
(One Gold)

22:57.350 --> 22:59.740
(One Gold)
Next time, "One Gold."

22:59.740 --> 23:01.050
(One Gold)
